Key Market Drivers
1. Rising Cardiovascular and Thrombotic Disease Burden
The prevalence of atrial fibrillation, deep‑vein thrombosis, and postoperative clotting complications continues to climb, expanding the patient pool that depends on reliable anticoagulation. Hospitals are compelled to maintain robust inventories of unfractionated heparin to support emergency and surgical protocols.
2. Clinical Preference for Rapid Reversibility
In high‑risk surgeries, the ability to neutralize anticoagulation swiftly with protamine remains a decisive factor. This clinical nuance preserves demand for Heparin Sodium Injection even as low‑molecular‑weight heparins gain traction for routine prophylaxis.
